{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PyszmHoV76mzDUKLUxCcp6","type":"tool_result","content":"# CSI Driver Deployment Quotes\n\n**(a) Recommended deployment mechanism:**\nUnder \"Deploying,\" the page states: \"Deploying a CSI driver onto Kubernetes is highlighted in detail in [_Recommended Mechanism for Deploying CSI Drivers on Kubernetes_]\"\n\n**(b) Controller plugin definition and location:**\nUnder \"Controller Plugin\": \"The controller component can be deployed as a Deployment or StatefulSet on any node in the cluster.\"\n\n**(c) Node plugin definition and location:**\nUnder \"Node Plugin\": \"The node component should be deployed on every node in the cluster through a DaemonSet.\"\n\n**(d) CSI drivers deployed with sidecar containers:**\nUnder \"Overview\": \"A CSI driver is typically deployed in Kubernetes as two components: a controller component and a per-node component. It consists of the CSI driver that implements the CSI Controller service and one or more [sidecar containers].\""}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ff5d535c-977f-479a-940c-05cafc9660f7","uuid":"f7ae5eec-71a7-4a73-ac1a-c4be873df950","timestamp":"2026-08-25T06:44:53.078Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":25879,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# CSI Driver Deployment Quotes\n\n**(a) Recommended deployment mechanism:**\nUnder \"Deploying,\" the page states: \"Deploying a CSI driver onto Kubernetes is highlighted in detail in [_Recommended Mechanism for Deploying CSI Drivers on Kubernetes_]\"\n\n**(b) Controller plugin definition and location:**\nUnder \"Controller Plugin\": \"The controller component can be deployed as a Deployment or StatefulSet on any node in the cluster.\"\n\n**(c) Node plugin definition and location:**\nUnder \"Node Plugin\": \"The node component should be deployed on every node in the cluster through a DaemonSet.\"\n\n**(d) CSI drivers deployed with sidecar containers:**\nUnder \"Overview\": \"A CSI driver is typically deployed in Kubernetes as two components: a controller component and a per-node component. It consists of the CSI driver that implements the CSI Controller service and one or more [sidecar containers].\"","durationMs":3179,"url":"https://kubernetes-csi.github.io/docs/deploying.html"}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AhEydNdPs7du95b8whsvsc","type":"tool_result","content":"# Container Storage Interface (CSI) Specification Transcription\n\nThe Container Storage Interface project presents the CSI specification and protobuf files. According to the documentation, \"This project contains the CSI specification and protobuf files.\"\n\nThe specification has gained significant adoption across multiple container orchestration platforms. The supported Container Orchestrators include Cloud Foundry, Kubernetes, Mesos, and Nomad, each offering their own CSI documentation and integration support.\n\nThe project maintains build status tracking through automated workflows, as indicated by the continuous integration badge displayed at the top of the README."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ff5d535c-977f-479a-940c-05cafc9660f7","uuid":"e8340457-a2b9-4d6a-9339-62335b188003","timestamp":"2026-08-25T06:44:53.757Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":599,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Container Storage Interface (CSI) Specification Transcription\n\nThe Container Storage Interface project presents the CSI specification and protobuf files. According to the documentation, \"This project contains the CSI specification and protobuf files.\"\n\nThe specification has gained significant adoption across multiple container orchestration platforms. The supported Container Orchestrators include Cloud Foundry, Kubernetes, Mesos, and Nomad, each offering their own CSI documentation and integration support.\n\nThe project maintains build status tracking through automated workflows, as indicated by the continuous integration badge displayed at the top of the README.","durationMs":2003,"url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/container-storage-interface/spec/master/README.md"}}
