{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DmQj5zRTnVC1D68ekwgduf","type":"tool_result","content":"# Exact Quotations from Kubernetes Volumes Documentation\n\n## emptyDir\n\n\"For a Pod that defines an `emptyDir` volume, the volume is created when the Pod is assigned to a node.\"\n\n\"As the name says, the `emptyDir` volume is initially empty.\"\n\n\"When a Pod is removed from a node for any reason, the data in the `emptyDir` is deleted permanently.\"\n\n\"A container crashing does _not_ remove a Pod from a node.\"\n\n\"The data in an `emptyDir` volume is safe across container crashes.\"\n\n\"If you set the `emptyDir.medium` field to `\"Memory\"`, Kubernetes mounts a tmpfs (RAM-backed filesystem) for you instead.\"\n\n\"While tmpfs is very fast, be aware that, unlike disks, files you write count against the memory limit of the container that wrote them.\"\n\n\"A size limit can be specified for the default medium, which limits the capacity of the `emptyDir` volume.\"\n\n## configMap\n\n\"A container using a ConfigMap as a [`subPath`](#using-subpath) volume mount will not receive updates when the ConfigMap changes.\"\n\n\"A ConfigMap is always mounted as `readOnly`.\"\n\n## secret\n\nI cannot provide an exact quotation for the secret volume type as the page content provided was truncated before reaching that section.\n\n## hostPath\n\nI cannot provide exact quotations for hostPath as the page content provided was truncated before reaching that section.\n\n## projected\n\nI cannot provide exact quotations as the page content provided was truncated before reaching that section.\n\n## downwardAPI\n\nI cannot provide exact quotations as the page content provided was truncated before reaching that section.\n\n## nfs\n\nI cannot provide exact quotations as the page content provided was truncated before reaching that section.\n\n## local\n\nI cannot provide exact quotations as the page content provided was truncated before reaching that section."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ff5d535c-977f-479a-940c-05cafc9660f7","uuid":"b9e89637-0fb5-4f7e-8a83-af247898f0bb","timestamp":"2026-08-25T06:46:02.981Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":605236,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Exact Quotations from Kubernetes Volumes Documentation\n\n## emptyDir\n\n\"For a Pod that defines an `emptyDir` volume, the volume is created when the Pod is assigned to a node.\"\n\n\"As the name says, the `emptyDir` volume is initially empty.\"\n\n\"When a Pod is removed from a node for any reason, the data in the `emptyDir` is deleted permanently.\"\n\n\"A container crashing does _not_ remove a Pod from a node.\"\n\n\"The data in an `emptyDir` volume is safe across container crashes.\"\n\n\"If you set the `emptyDir.medium` field to `\"Memory\"`, Kubernetes mounts a tmpfs (RAM-backed filesystem) for you instead.\"\n\n\"While tmpfs is very fast, be aware that, unlike disks, files you write count against the memory limit of the container that wrote them.\"\n\n\"A size limit can be specified for the default medium, which limits the capacity of the `emptyDir` volume.\"\n\n## configMap\n\n\"A container using a ConfigMap as a [`subPath`](#using-subpath) volume mount will not receive updates when the ConfigMap changes.\"\n\n\"A ConfigMap is always mounted as `readOnly`.\"\n\n## secret\n\nI cannot provide an exact quotation for the secret volume type as the page content provided was truncated before reaching that section.\n\n## hostPath\n\nI cannot provide exact quotations for hostPath as the page content provided was truncated before reaching that section.\n\n## projected\n\nI cannot provide exact quotations as the page content provided was truncated before reaching that section.\n\n## downwardAPI\n\nI cannot provide exact quotations as the page content provided was truncated before reaching that section.\n\n## nfs\n\nI cannot provide exact quotations as the page content provided was truncated before reaching that section.\n\n## local\n\nI cannot provide exact quotations as the page content provided was truncated before reaching that section.","durationMs":5315,"url":"https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/storage/volumes/"}}
