{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SL7sHpmdZr2dByoBbVU4mP","type":"tool_result","content":"# CSIDriver API Reference Quotations\n\n**CSIDriver (top-level description):**\n\"CSIDriver captures information about a Container Storage Interface (CSI) volume driver deployed on the cluster.\"\n\n**spec.attachRequired:**\n\"attachRequired indicates this CSI volume driver requires an attach operation (because it implements the CSI ControllerPublishVolume() method)\"\n\n**spec.podInfoOnMount:**\n\"podInfoOnMount indicates this CSI volume driver requires additional pod information (like podName, podUID, etc.) during mount operations\"\n\n**spec.volumeLifecycleModes:**\n\"volumeLifecycleModes defines what kind of volumes this CSI volume driver supports. The default if the list is empty is 'Persistent', which is the usage defined by the CSI specification and implemented in Kubernetes via the usual PV/PVC mechanism. The other mode is 'Ephemeral'. In this mode, volumes are defined inline inside the pod spec with CSIVolumeSource and their lifecycle is tied to the lifecycle of that pod.\""}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ff5d535c-977f-479a-940c-05cafc9660f7","uuid":"3b12c5ca-5875-432f-8daf-ae2806aa8a38","timestamp":"2026-08-25T06:48:28.768Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":553448,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# CSIDriver API Reference Quotations\n\n**CSIDriver (top-level description):**\n\"CSIDriver captures information about a Container Storage Interface (CSI) volume driver deployed on the cluster.\"\n\n**spec.attachRequired:**\n\"attachRequired indicates this CSI volume driver requires an attach operation (because it implements the CSI ControllerPublishVolume() method)\"\n\n**spec.podInfoOnMount:**\n\"podInfoOnMount indicates this CSI volume driver requires additional pod information (like podName, podUID, etc.) during mount operations\"\n\n**spec.volumeLifecycleModes:**\n\"volumeLifecycleModes defines what kind of volumes this CSI volume driver supports. The default if the list is empty is 'Persistent', which is the usage defined by the CSI specification and implemented in Kubernetes via the usual PV/PVC mechanism. The other mode is 'Ephemeral'. In this mode, volumes are defined inline inside the pod spec with CSIVolumeSource and their lifecycle is tied to the lifecycle of that pod.\"","durationMs":3357,"url":"https://kubernetes.io/docs/reference/kubernetes-api/config-and-storage-resources/csi-driver-v1/"}}
